  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GLoBe S&#xE9;n&#xE9;gal - Des collectivit&#xE9;s territoriales fortes et une intercommunalit&#xE9; forte mettent en &#x153;uvre des strat&#xE9;gies participatives et durables par rapport &#xE0; l&apos;&#xE9;conomie locale et la gestion des d&#xE9;chets avec une attention particuli&#xE8;re aux femmes et jeunes</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Des collectivit&#xE9;s territoriales fortes et une intercommunalit&#xE9; forte mettent en &#x153;uvre des strat&#xE9;gies participatives et durables par rapport &#xE0; l&apos;&#xE9;conomie locale et la gestion des d&#xE9;chets avec une attention particuli&#xE8;re aux femmes et aux jeunes.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program directly targets local politicians, civil servants and key figures of the civil society who play a facilitating role for good local governance that contributes to improved living conditions for the most vulnerable. GLoBe in Senegal directly reaches 372 politicians and civil servants and 374 key figures from civil society. The beneficiaries are the inhabitants of the municipalities of Tambacounda, Sokone, Keur Moussa, Pout and Diender, with special attention to the most vulnerable.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">VVSG&#x2019;s program &#x2018;GLoBe&#x2019; (Goed Lokaal Bestuur) is committed to good local governance for sustainable and coherent policies. Local governments can play an important role as duty bearers to contribute to safeguarding the human rights of their populations, to contribute to the realization of the SDGs and to improve living conditions for the population. In Senegal, GLoBe supports local governments developing qualitative and inclusive policies for local economy and waste management. Special attention is given to environmentally friendly solutions (reduction, recycling and valorisation of waste and the development of a green local economy through organic farming, composting and the promotion of environmental standards and labels) and to women, youth, farmers and small entrepreneurs to strengthen participation of the most vulnerable in local government&#x2019;s actions. By strengthening local governance on economic development and waste, GLoBe in Senegal advances healthier and cleaner living environme...(+3 characters extra in FundHub text)</narrative>
  </description>
